    <briefdescription>
<para>A class which implements a gyrokinetic Poisson bracket operator. The implemented equation is: <formula id="342">$ \{F, G\} = b\dot(\nabla F \cross \nabla G) $</formula> with <formula id="343">$ b= \mathbf{B} / B $</formula> the unitary magnetic field, i.e: <formula id="344">$ \{F, G\} = {\cal J}_{\rm x}^{-1}\epsilon^{ijk}\partial_{x^i} F \partial_{x^j} G b_k $</formula> with <formula id="336">$ {\cal J}_{\rm x} $</formula> the jacobian of the system, <formula id="345">$ b_k $</formula> the covariant components of b and <formula id="346">$\epsilon^{ijk} $</formula> the Levi-Civita symbol. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Mapping3D</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A type representing a mapping in 3 dimensions. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MappingCoord</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the coordinate that will be used to evaluate the mapping. This coordinate is used to calculate the determinant of the Jacobian and the metric tensor. It is almost always equal to the argument type of the 3D mapping but axi-symmetry may make it useful to evaluate the mapping on a coordinate with a reduced dimensionality. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MetricTensorType</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>A type which provides the metric tensor at a coordinate of type MappingCoord. By default it is calculated from the Jacobian of the mapping using a <ref refid="classMetricTensorEvaluator" kindref="compound">MetricTensorEvaluator</ref>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
